{
  "core_message": "Sickle cell disease is a genetic blood disorder where red blood cells change shape, blocking vessels and causing pain.",
  "mood": "curious",
  "title": "7.7 million people live with blood cells that turn into crescents",
  "description": "Sickle cell disease is a genetic condition affecting millions worldwide. It causes red blood cells to twist into rigid, crescent shapes that clog tiny blood vessels. This video explains the mechanics of the blockage and the real-world impact of this inherited trait.\n\nKey points:\n- Caused by an abnormal beta-globin gene inherited from both parents.\n- Rigidity prevents cells from squeezing through capillaries.\n- Affects about 7.7 million people globally.\n\nBased on the Wikipedia article \"Sickle cell disease\" (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sickle_cell_disease), licensed CC BY-SA 4.0.",
